    "title": "<p>Differential diagnoses for nodal T&nbsp;follicular helper (TFH) cell lymphoma, follicular type (nTFHL-F)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Ming-Qinq Du",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 707.1pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"943\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 81.5pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">nTFHL-F growth pattern</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 81.55pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mimic</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 544.05pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"725\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Key features for differential diagnosis (integrated approach required)<sup>a</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 81.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Follicular lymphoma&ndash;like</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 81.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Follicular lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 544.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"725\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">nTFHL-F:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Comparison of CD10 and other TFH stains with CD20 shows that CD10+ cells are T&nbsp;cells; CD10/PAX5 double immunostaining may help</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 81.5pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTGC-like</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 81.55pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Classic Hodgkin lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 544.05pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"725\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">nTFHL-F:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HRS-like cells usually display a relatively intact B-cell programme (not always)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HRS-like cells rosetted by neoplastic T&nbsp;cells with TFH phenotype (CD10, if positive, is most helpful)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Classic Hodgkin lymphoma:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Favoured if a mediastinal mass is present</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Crippled B-cell programme in HRS cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4+ T-cell rosettes may show weak to moderate (but not strong) PD1 expression and are CD10&minus; </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{28893733}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTGC, progressive transformation of germinal centres.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Flow</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> cytometry dim sCD3 and CD4+/CD10+ or CD4+/PD1+ T&nbsp;cells and detection of clonal TR (TCR) gene rearrangement and/or <em>RHOA</em> p.G17V point to nTFHL-F.</span></p>",
